---
import Base from '~/layouts/Base.astro';
import { t, CONTACT_EMAIL } from '~/i18n/strings';

const lang = 'en';
const s = t(lang);
const lastUpdated = s.privacy.lastUpdated.replace('{date}', '18 October 2026');
---
<Base
  lang={lang}
  path="/privacy"
  title="Privacy policy — FreshGarant"
  description="How FreshGarant handles your data. In plain language."
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <span class="section-kicker">{s.privacy.heroKicker}</span>
      <h1>{s.privacy.heroTitle}</h1>
      <p style="color: var(--fg-text-faint); font-size: 13px;">{lastUpdated}</p>
      <p class="section-sub" style="margin-top: 20px;">{s.privacy.intro}</p>

      <article class="prose">
        <h2>1. Who we are</h2>
        <p>
          FreshGarant is published by <strong>Grounded Studio</strong>, based in the
          Netherlands. Contact: <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>.
          For privacy-specific requests, email the same address with
          "Privacy request" in the subject.
        </p>

        <h2>2. What stays on your device</h2>
        <p>
          <strong>Everything by default.</strong> The product list,
          categories, storage locations, expiry dates, prices, consumption
          history, waste log, shopping list, achievements, settings — all of
          it is stored in a local SQLite database on your phone.
          We never see it.
        </p>

        <h2>3. What leaves your device, and why</h2>

        <h3>3.1 Firebase Analytics (anonymous usage data)</h3>
        <p>
          We log a small set of events to understand which parts of the app
          are used — for example, which screens are opened, which features
          get tapped, whether a purchase succeeded. We deliberately send
          <strong>no personally identifying information, no product names,
          no photo contents, no receipt text</strong>. All quantities are
          bucketed into ranges (e.g. "5–15 items") so we can read trends
          without identifying individuals.
        </p>
        <p>
          Processor: Google (Firebase).
          Legal basis: legitimate interest in understanding product usage.
          You can opt out by denying analytics permission in your Android
          system settings.
        </p>

        <h3>3.2 Gemini API — only when you use an AI feature</h3>
        <p>
          When you tap AI Fridge Scan, AI Recipe or AI Weekly Meal Plan,
          the following is sent to Google's Gemini API:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Fridge scan:</strong> the photo you just took.</li>
          <li><strong>Recipe / meal plan:</strong> a list of product names
            currently in your inventory.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Google processes these to generate a response and then returns it
          to the app. Per Google's current terms, data sent to the paid
          Gemini API is not used to train Google's models. We never store
          the photo on our servers (we don't have servers) — it travels
          phone → Google → phone.
        </p>
        <p>
          Receipt scan uses Google's on-device ML Kit, which runs locally
          on your phone. Nothing leaves your device.
        </p>

        <h3>3.3 Family sharing (opt-in, Firestore)</h3>
        <p>
          If you create or join a family, the products you add become
          visible to the other family members via Google Cloud Firestore.
          You can leave the family at any time, after which your products
          stop syncing. Family data is deleted from Firestore 30 days after
          the last family member leaves.
        </p>

        <h3>3.4 Barcode lookups (Open Food Facts)</h3>
        <p>
          When you scan a barcode we query the free
          <a href="https://openfoodfacts.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open Food Facts</a>
          database for product name, brand and nutrition info. Only the
          barcode number is sent — no identifying information about you.
        </p>

        <h3>3.5 Google Play Billing (if you buy PRO)</h3>
        <p>
          Payment is handled entirely by Google Play. We receive only a
          confirmation that your subscription is active or inactive — no
          card details, no billing address.
        </p>

        <h3>3.6 Location (only if you enable "Nearby store alerts")</h3>
        <p>
          If you opt in to nearby-store notifications, your foreground
          location is read when the app is open to compare against your
          saved supermarkets. Location is never sent to our servers, never
          stored, and never used in the background.
        </p>

        <h2>4. What we do NOT collect</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>No account, email or password is required to use the app.</li>
          <li>No contacts, calendar, SMS or microphone access.</li>
          <li>No advertising identifiers for ad-targeting purposes.</li>
          <li>No third-party advertising SDKs. There are no ads in FreshGarant.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>5. Your rights (GDPR / UK GDPR)</h2>
        <p>You have the right to:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Request a copy of what we hold about you (export your product
            list from Settings → Data → Export CSV; the only cloud data is
            family-shared products, available via the family screen).</li>
          <li>Delete all local data from Settings → Data → Delete all data.
            This clears the SQLite database and all SharedPreferences.</li>
          <li>Request deletion of any Firebase Analytics records associated
            with your Firebase install-ID by emailing us.</li>
          <li>Withdraw consent for analytics or location at any time via
            Android system settings.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>6. Data retention</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Local SQLite data: retained until you delete it (uninstalling
            the app or using Settings → Delete all data).</li>
          <li>Firebase Analytics: retained per Firebase defaults (max 14
            months) and anonymised earlier where possible.</li>
          <li>Family-shared Firestore data: deleted 30 days after the last
            member leaves the family.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>7. Children</h2>
        <p>
          FreshGarant is not directed at children under 13 (16 in the EU).
          We do not knowingly collect data from children. If you believe a
          child has used the app and you want their data removed, email us.
        </p>

        <h2>8. Changes to this policy</h2>
        <p>
          If we make material changes we will update the "last updated"
          date and, where appropriate, show an in-app notice on next
          launch. Continued use of the app constitutes acceptance.
        </p>

        <h2>9. Contact</h2>
        <p>
          Questions, concerns, or formal privacy requests:
          <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
